TRADING RULEBOOK

1. Trade in the direction of the dominant higher-timeframe trend.
2. The daily chart controls trade bias.
3. The 4H chart confirms market structure.
4. The 1H chart is used for entry timing.
5. Long trades are favored when price is above EMA 20, EMA 50, and EMA 200.
6. Short trades are favored when price is below EMA 20, EMA 50, and EMA 200.
7. Avoid buying directly into major resistance.
8. Avoid selling directly into major support.
9. RSI above 70 warns of overbought conditions.
10. RSI below 30 warns of oversold conditions.
11. ATR should be used to place stops outside normal volatility.
12. A strong setup should have at least 2:1 reward-to-risk.
13. Pullback entries are generally better than chasing extended moves.
14. Breakout trades need confirmation beyond resistance or support.
15. Candlestick confirmation improves entry quality.
16. If higher timeframes disagree, reduce confidence or avoid the trade.
17. The setup is invalid if price breaks the structure supporting the trade.
18. No trade is better than forcing a weak setup.
